From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:05:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/26] tools: add rdgen-github-bootstrap (private build repo
 setup and upstream updates)

Python (stdlib + requests + PyNaCl; py3-pynacl 1.6.2 on Alpine 3.24,
python3-nacl 1.5.0 on Debian 13).

  check-token  what the token can see (repo, private/fork, Actions,
               Secrets, Administration read)
  init         build the tree (upstream master + patch series + pullify)
               or take a prepared one; create the PRIVATE repo if the token
               may (else explain the one manual click); refuse forks and
               public repos; push; check that the branch is the default
               branch (workflow_dispatch needs that); set the ZIP_PASSWORD
               Actions secret with a libsodium sealed box against the
               repo's public key; enable Actions if needed and allowed;
               wait until the five generator workflows are registered
  set-secret   re-set ZIP_PASSWORD (rotation)
  update       ls-remote upstream; if it moved, rebuild: git am -3 every
               patch except the ones with the "Rdgen-Mechanical: pullify"
               trailer, then run tools/pullify.py instead of those. Verify
               with compileall, pullify --check, manage.py check and
               makemigrations --check. Push only with --apply. If any step
               fails, nothing is pushed, the current version stays, and the
               error is reported (exit 4; optionally through
               rustdesk-notify with --notify).

Secrets never go on argv. Tokens are read from --token-file (a warning if
it is group/other readable) or --token-stdin. git gets the token as an
http extraheader through GIT_CONFIG_{COUNT,KEY_n,VALUE_n} environment
variables of the child process, scoped to the push URL's origin and
with the credential helper disabled, so it is not in the URL, argv,
.git/config or a credential store. The state (upstream and pushed shas,
branch) is kept in /etc/rdgen/bootstrap.json (0600).

